      "message": "yeah true, I wanted to do this but could not find a good way to do this as we do not have a device layer framework in pkvm. During pkvm initialization, we could go through the PCI devices and create a snapshot of existing devices, but then we leave it vulnerable for hotplug devices. For 6.18, I was planning to have a thin device layer that caches device specific details that are security related.\n\nFor 6.12, would it make sense to do it always - this is not on a hot path(context tear down and pasid table tear down) so it should be okay I guess. What do you think?",
